                           :history [["+" "0.0-1853"]],
                           :type "syntax",
                           :full-name-encode "syntax/deref",
                           :extra-sources ({:code "(defn- macros [ch]\n  (case ch\n    \\\" read-string*\n    \\: read-keyword\n    \\; read-comment\n    \\' (wrapping-reader 'quote)\n    \\@ (wrapping-reader 'clojure.core/deref)\n    \\^ read-meta\n    \\` read-syntax-quote ;;(wrapping-reader 'syntax-quote)\n    \\~ read-unquote\n    \\( read-list\n    \\) read-unmatched-delimiter\n    \\[ read-vector\n    \\] read-unmatched-delimiter\n    \\{ read-map\n    \\} read-unmatched-delimiter\n    \\\\ read-char*\n    \\% read-arg\n    \\# read-dispatch\n    nil))",
                                            :title "Reader table",
                                            :repo "tools.reader",
                                            :tag "v1.3.6",
                                            :filename "src/main/clojure/clojure/tools/reader.clj",
                                            :lines [788 807],
                                            :url "https://github.com/clojure/tools.reader/blob/v1.3.6/src/main/clojure/clojure/tools/reader.clj#L788-L807"}),
                           :summary "Get the value that a reference is currently referring to.  A \"reference\" can\nbe a [`atom`][doc:cljs.core/atom], [`delay`][doc:cljs.core/delay], or [`var`][doc:cljs.core/var].\n\n- `@foo` - `(deref foo)`",
                           :details "`@foo` is sugar for [`(deref foo)`][doc:cljs.core/deref].",
                           :examples "Quote the form to see how the reader expands it:\n\n```clj\n'@foo\n;;=> (clojure.core/deref foo)\n```\n\nAn [`atom`][doc:cljs.core/atom] is a mutable reference to an immutable value.\n\n```clj\n(def a (atom 1))\n@a\n;;=> 1\n\n(reset! a 2)\n@a\n;;=> 2\n```\n\nA [`delay`][doc:cljs.core/delay] will evaluate by executing the given expression\nthe first time it is dereferenced.\n\n```clj\n(def a (delay (do (println \"delayed.\") 1)))\n@a\n;; prints:\n;;  delayed.\n;;=> 1\n\n@a\n;;=> 1\n```\n\nEvaluating a symbol naturally dereferences the value of a [`var`][doc:cljs.core/var].\nBut a var reference can be dereferenced as a roundabout way to obtain its value.\n(Var references are mainly used to retrieve metadata on that var).\n\n```clj\n(def ^{:doc \"my var\"} a 1)\n(:doc (meta #'a))\n;;=> \"my var\"\n\n(deref (var a))\n;;=> 1\n\n;; combining shorthand forms instead\n@#'a\n;;=> 1\n```",
                           :full-name "syntax/deref",
                           :see-also ["cljs.core/deref"
                                      "cljs.core/atom"
                                      "cljs.core/delay"]},
